(1055558, 126581, 22479, '<td valign="top">What I like about this shot is the pose of Toto. She appears to be intently watching the road, and that adds much interest to this shot. There''s a little bit of haloing around the heels of the ruby shoes but not quite enough to be distracting. I think your color balance is excellent too. Overall a great shot. 8</td>', 'What I like about this shot is the pose of Toto. She appears to be intently watching the road, and that adds much interest to this shot. There''s a little bit of haloing around the heels of the ruby shoes but not quite enough to be distracting. I think your color balance is excellent too. Overall a great shot. 8', '2004-12-10 02:42:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055559, 126062, 22479, '<td valign="top">...eat the lemon? :)    (revisiting this photograph for comments)<br/> <br/>Quite a motivational message here. I like the way you framed this shot. The lighting works well. Black backdrop certainly cuts out the distractions and allows the viewer to focus on the message at hand. Overall well done in my book. 7</td>', '...eat the lemon? :)    (revisiting this photograph for comments) Quite a motivational message here. I like the way you framed this shot. The lighting works well. Black backdrop certainly cuts out the distractions and allows the viewer to focus on the message at hand. Overall well done in my book. 7', '2004-12-10 02:44:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055562, 126800, 22479, '<td valign="top">Haha, chillin'' in dish of...gatorade? jello? funky blue liquid? <br/> <br/>I think your choice of colors here works well. My only concern is that your duck appears to be reflecting too much of the blue juice. Perhaps if you illuminated this side of the duck with a directed diffuse light, he would be better exposed...just a thought. Bumping this one up to a 6.</td>', 'Haha, chillin'' in dish of...gatorade? jello? funky blue liquid?  I think your choice of colors here works well. My only concern is that your duck appears to be reflecting too much of the blue juice. Perhaps if you illuminated this side of the duck with a directed diffuse light, he would be better exposed...just a thought. Bumping this one up to a 6.', '2004-12-10 02:50:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055564, 126713, 22479, '<td valign="top">Revisiting this shot as it bears some interest for me.<br/> <br/>I like your composition. Nice and clean, well exposed. Specimens...interesting title. Even more interesting to contemplate what specimens these represent. Bumping this one up.</td>', 'Revisiting this shot as it bears some interest for me. I like your composition. Nice and clean, well exposed. Specimens...interesting title. Even more interesting to contemplate what specimens these represent. Bumping this one up.', '2004-12-10 02:53:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055565, 126629, 22479, '<td valign="top">Couple of issues here which make this photograph unacceptable to me. Size: try to submit something more sbustantial in size...try to shoot for 600-640 pixels on the long side. Artistically I think you took a lot of liberties in designating this as a Christmas glow. Reason why I feel this way is that by glancing at this photo, I''m not exactly sure what I''m looking at. I can''t even begin to imagine what this is supposed to be. So I''ll trust that it has something to do with Christmas. <br/> <br/>From a technical standpoint, there is no indication here of any type of focus. I could have reproduced this by using photoshop and the brush tool. Sorry but I cannot score this very well.</td>', 'Couple of issues here which make this photograph unacceptable to me. Size: try to submit something more sbustantial in size...try to shoot for 600-640 pixels on the long side. Artistically I think you took a lot of liberties in designating this as a Christmas glow. Reason why I feel this way is that by glancing at this photo, I''m not exactly sure what I''m looking at. I can''t even begin to imagine what this is supposed to be. So I''ll trust that it has something to do with Christmas.  From a technical standpoint, there is no indication here of any type of focus. I could have reproduced this by using photoshop and the brush tool. Sorry but I cannot score this very well.', '2004-12-10 02:58:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055566, 126423, 23458, '<td valign="top">Now that is one stunning flower macro, DOF is fantastic.  Border is not (the yellow is just not working). Now normally I''d look at a flower macro and think to myself "that person knows how to use their camera and has found themselves a pretty flower.... so what ? But, thanks to the aforementioned terrific DOF this image transcends that typical sentiment and earns you a big fat 10. <br/> <br/>Great work.</td>', 'Now that is one stunning flower macro, DOF is fantastic.  Border is not (the yellow is just not working). Now normally I''d look at a flower macro and think to myself "that person knows how to use their camera and has found themselves a pretty flower.... so what ? But, thanks to the aforementioned terrific DOF this image transcends that typical sentiment and earns you a big fat 10.  Great work.', '2004-12-10 02:59:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055567, 126450, 23458, '<td valign="top">This is a nice approach, the silhouette is great - terrific lighting. I think you would do a little better in this particular challenge if the lemons were a little more vibrant, as it is the colour yellow isn''t quite creating the impact of the photo. 6</td>', 'This is a nice approach, the silhouette is great - terrific lighting. I think you would do a little better in this particular challenge if the lemons were a little more vibrant, as it is the colour yellow isn''t quite creating the impact of the photo. 6', '2004-12-10 03:00:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055568, 126822, 22479, '<td valign="top">Interesting image. I think you took a regular photograph and tweaked the colors to turn everything yellow. Two comments. Rather then being yellow, it''s more of a muddy mustard color. There is a also a distracting lack of contrast and focus which takes away from the beauty of what you are trying to portray. For all the processing you performed, you kept the sky relatively blue, and I''ll give ya bonus points for that.</td>', 'Interesting image. I think you took a regular photograph and tweaked the colors to turn everything yellow. Two comments. Rather then being yellow, it''s more of a muddy mustard color. There is a also a distracting lack of contrast and focus which takes away from the beauty of what you are trying to portray. For all the processing you performed, you kept the sky relatively blue, and I''ll give ya bonus points for that.', '2004-12-10 03:02:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055569, 126601, 23458, '<td valign="top">wow... that would have been a pain in the ass to clean up, I hope you didn''t have to shoot too many. It''s a great Idea, but technically not quite there for mine. The lighting is a bit off and the backdrop would be more effective without the strange pink tone. Also, I would prefer to be slightly close to the action. 6.</td>', 'wow... that would have been a pain in the ass to clean up, I hope you didn''t have to shoot too many. It''s a great Idea, but technically not quite there for mine. The lighting is a bit off and the backdrop would be more effective without the strange pink tone. Also, I would prefer to be slightly close to the action. 6.', '2004-12-10 03:02:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055571, 125618, 22479, '<td valign="top">Cute pooch. Two comments. Size really should be larger...try to submit a photograph that measures between 600-640 pixels on the long edge. Other comment is that while the focus appears to be sharp, there are aliasing artifacts (stair-stepping jaggies) on the deck boards which is a result of either resizing the photograph without using a bicubic or equivalent algorithm, or by cranking the sharpness up too high. These two issues mainly detract from the beauty of this photograph. Sorry.</td>', 'Cute pooch. Two comments. Size really should be larger...try to submit a photograph that measures between 600-640 pixels on the long edge. Other comment is that while the focus appears to be sharp, there are aliasing artifacts (stair-stepping jaggies) on the deck boards which is a result of either resizing the photograph without using a bicubic or equivalent algorithm, or by cranking the sharpness up too high. These two issues mainly detract from the beauty of this photograph. Sorry.', '2004-12-10 03:06:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055573, 126387, 17507, '<td valign="top">nice lighting.  best one i''ve seen so far from the pix i''ve rated.</td>', 'nice lighting.  best one i''ve seen so far from the pix i''ve rated.', '2004-12-10 03:12:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055574, 125417, 22479, '<td valign="top">A bold entry. This shot has a lot of artistic strengths. It''s probably gonna get shot down for a couple of reasons. First is that I suspect this will be too erotic for some people''s taste. Second is that this is merely a desaturated and yellow toned image which makes no connection with the color yellow in an interpretive manner. I think this would be equally suited in a steel blue tone, sepia tone, or pure B&amp;W (or in color). It''s as if it was toned yellow just to submit for this challenge. For me, it''s the second reason why I cannot highly rate this otherwise technically and artistically superb entry.</td>', 'A bold entry. This shot has a lot of artistic strengths. It''s probably gonna get shot down for a couple of reasons. First is that I suspect this will be too erotic for some people''s taste. Second is that this is merely a desaturated and yellow toned image which makes no connection with the color yellow in an interpretive manner. I think this would be equally suited in a steel blue tone, sepia tone, or pure B&W (or in color). It''s as if it was toned yellow just to submit for this challenge. For me, it''s the second reason why I cannot highly rate this otherwise technically and artistically superb entry.', '2004-12-10 03:13:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1055576, 126725, 22479, '<td valign="top">Okay. Three comments. <br/> <br/>1) Title is almost appropriate for the designated photograph, afterall, bananas are yellow, as is this shot. It could have been more relevant if there was ACTUALLY a banana somewhere in this photo. But you were being subtle right?<br/> <br/>2) What am I looking at? Is this a part of a ceiling, or a wall? Looks like there is a pin hole over on the left side which gives some clue. <br/> <br/>3) The only relevance of this entry to this particular challenge is that yes, everything in this shot is yellow. So what''s the catch? Is there some inner meaning here that I''m too dense to comprehend? Sorry.<br/></td>', 'Okay. Three comments.  1) Title is almost appropriate for the designated photograph, afterall, bananas are yellow, as is this shot. It could have been more relevant if there was ACTUALLY a banana somewhere in this photo. But you were being subtle right? 2) What am I looking at? Is this a part of a ceiling, or a wall? Looks like there is a pin hole over on the left side which gives some clue.  3) The only relevance of this entry to this particular challenge is that yes, everything in this shot is yellow. So what''s the catch? Is there some inner meaning here that I''m too dense to comprehend? Sorry.', '2004-12-10 03:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
