(1063747, 126225, 27421, '<td valign="top">My first challenge. Overall I am happy with the results. My main focus was to capture the spirit of the challenge, more so than produce a technically and photographically noteworthy submission. I realize all aspects affect the votes and opinions though, and will strive to improve for future challenges.<br/> <br/>Now, in answer to the questions, the car lights on indicate someone coming back to the Rose (revisited :) )... I like the subdued surroundings of the sign, since many parts of society insist men sneak around to visit strip clubs... just an instantaneous thought in determining my subject, and the rest is part of snap decision to take a "snap-shot".............</td>', 'My first challenge. Overall I am happy with the results. My main focus was to capture the spirit of the challenge, more so than produce a technically and photographically noteworthy submission. I realize all aspects affect the votes and opinions though, and will strive to improve for future challenges. Now, in answer to the questions, the car lights on indicate someone coming back to the Rose (revisited :) )... I like the subdued surroundings of the sign, since many parts of society insist men sneak around to visit strip clubs... just an instantaneous thought in determining my subject, and the rest is part of snap decision to take a "snap-shot".............', '2004-12-15 09:22:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1063748, 126539, 2741, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 10. I thought this was well executed, and well balanced.</td>', 'I gave this a 10. I thought this was well executed, and well balanced.', '2004-12-15 09:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1063752, 126461, 16739, '<td valign="top">though for sure you were a winner , sorry</td>', 'though for sure you were a winner , sorry', '2004-12-15 09:25:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1063759, 126788, 29443, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments! This was a 15 sec exposure of an unlighted candle with a small light behind it for illumination. I then quickly "drew" each trail with a small yellow light, turned it on at the candle, off at the coin. A second momentary "dab" at each coin to blend. More then a few attempts to get it balanced!<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments! This was a 15 sec exposure of an unlighted candle with a small light behind it for illumination. I then quickly "drew" each trail with a small yellow light, turned it on at the candle, off at the coin. A second momentary "dab" at each coin to blend. More then a few attempts to get it balanced!', '2004-12-15 09:29:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1063766, 126703, 17505, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m disappointed! This is one of the three photo''s I''d rated a 10 and I really though it would rank much higher. Bummer! I stand by my vote. Excellent concept and execution!</td>', 'Wow, I''m disappointed! This is one of the three photo''s I''d rated a 10 and I really though it would rank much higher. Bummer! I stand by my vote. Excellent concept and execution!', '2004-12-15 09:35:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1063773, 126581, 17203, '<td valign="top">Cairn Terriers are a difficult prop to build when you don''t have one handy. As noted, the socks should have been blue, too. Oh, well. I did what I could with the materials available to me, so I can''t complain. ;-)</td>', 'Cairn Terriers are a difficult prop to build when you don''t have one handy. As noted, the socks should have been blue, too. Oh, well. I did what I could with the materials available to me, so I can''t complain. ;-)', '2004-12-15 09:38:59.000000', NULL, 0),
